            "description": "OTHER_INFO is optional JSON with schema_version=1, estimates.budget and estimates.duration_days (low/recommended/high; currency or day_basis), scenarios.without_ai and scenarios.with_ai (each with estimates and confidence), selected_scenario (without_ai|with_ai|null), phases, confidence, item_confidence, baseline, assumptions, unverified, guide_version and review_status. confidence is an object {score: number 0..100, basis: non-empty string, evidence_level: requirements|design|first_code|verified_code}; each item_confidence entry adds dev_item_id. Only top-level estimates and the selected scenario recommended values must match table forecasts; unselected scenario estimates remain independent. If undecided, leave representative forecast columns null. Optional forecast columns contain report representative values, not customer limits. Store item scenario estimates in RESOURCE_FORECAST.scenarios.without_ai and .with_ai, and report totals/evidence in OTHER_INFO.scenarios with the same keys. Keep the full comparison table in ANALYSIS_CONTENT as Markdown. Use the same currency, rates and duration day_basis across scenarios, explicitly explaining any differences."
